children.details:
Besides `id`, `title` and `at`: `icon`, a one-line `description`, either `children` or `details` (Markdown text the block opens into instead) and `meta` for data of other tools. Ids are stable, so links and comments can rely on them.

```json
{
  "takesix": "1.0",
  "title": "Payments",
  "blocks": [
    { "id": "api", "title": "API", "at": "A1:B2" },
    { "id": "bank", "title": "Bank", "at": "E1:F2" }
  ],
  "links": [{ "from": "api", "to": "bank" }]
}
```
Full specification: [FORMAT.md](https://github.com/vvapnik/takesix-core/blob/main/FORMAT.md)

Columns A–F, rows 1–6, both corners included: `"at": "A1:C2"` is three columns by two rows, `"B3"` one cell.

- blocks never overlap;
- empty cells are space: linked blocks keep a free row or column between them;
- a level reads row by row, left to right.

On phones empty rows and columns shrink away.
